{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1531906-new-to-pugmire-where-to-start","id":1531906,"title":"New to Pugmire. Where to start?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-03T11:11:25-08:00","id":1531906,"title":"New to Pugmire. Where to start?","content":"Hello, I\u2019m new to Pugmire and getting a game together. So far I have the first edition book. I\u2019m looking into the adventures but not sure where to start? Any help is greatly appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28391-shoyu","name":"Shoyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28391_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T11:50:42-08:00","id":1531909,"title":"","content":"Are you more interested in stories of Dogs (<b>Pugmire</b>), Cats ( <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> ), Rats and Mouse ( <b>Squeeks in the Deep</b> ) - or pirates and/or Reptiles and Birds (<b> Pirates of Pugmire</b> )? In bracets I written names of (core)books about those Species. <br /> <br /> If you are interested in Dogs, there is full cool jumpstart for them - <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/239620/Pans-Guide-for-New-Pioneers\" target=\"_blank\"><i><b>Pan's Guide for New Pioneers</b></i></a> - Other Species have other starting adventure/books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T11:53:13-08:00","id":1531911,"title":"","content":"Mostly dogs right now, since that\u2019s the book I have. But next check I\u2019m looking at the pirate books. Thanks for the link I\u2019m taking a look right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28391-shoyu","user":"Shoyu","date":". 03-14-2024, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28391-shoyu","name":"Shoyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28391_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T14:05:05-08:00","id":1531923,"title":"","content":"To correct a bit:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/232337/the-secret-of-vinsen-s-tomb-a-pugmire-jumpstart\" target=\"_blank\">The Secret of Vinsen's Tomb</a> is the official jump start book. It has the basic rules in it, and is a decent starter adventure meant for people trying out the game for the first time (esp. if at least the GM is familiar with D&amp;D or similar RPGs).<br /> <br /> Pan's Guide for New Pioneers is definitely a book you want if you're just starting though, as it's a much more thorough in explaining the logic of the adventure and encounters to a new GM.<br /> <br /> That said, Pirates of Pugmire also contains a three-part adventure series in it that you can play while just sticking to dogs (at least for the players); using the new Callings isn't even necessary. Sunken Bones is an additional sample adventure you can get that uses Pirates, but like Pirates the players can stick to the Pugmire core book material.<br /> <br /> You can also peruse <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/cc/17/Canis-Minor\" target=\"_blank\">Canis Minor</a>, the Realms of Pugmire community content page. While not official material, there are plenty of adventures in there you could take a look at if you don't want to take a stab at creating your own things yet.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T16:32:56-08:00","id":1531932,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve just put the Pan book at the top of my list! Thank you for the suggestion. It looks perfect to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28391-shoyu","name":"Shoyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28391_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T21:34:48-08:00","id":1531943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1531906-new-to-pugmire-where-to-start?p=1531923#post1531923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To correct a bit:</div> </div> </div> </div>To extend what <b>Heavy Arms</b> written - For Cats, <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> corebook has 1 adventure. There is also official 3 stories 'adventure path'/campaign in <a href=\"http://Adventures%20for%20Curious%20Cats\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Adventures for Curios Cats</b></a> - I can recommend those, run it and it's generally a cool bundle of cat fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Right now there is also crowdfunding for <a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/projects/onyx-path/curious-cats-of-mau\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Curios Cats of Mau</b></a>, i.e. <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> 2E de facto - which also will have 3 stories to run and you can get those in time of crowdfunding even - but book will need <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> 2E corebook, that is de facto <b>Pugmire</b> 2E corebook ( with added simple conversions for all canon Species as the time of 2E start ). Both <b>Curios Cats</b> and <b>Realms of Pugmire </b>are books in production, but you already have text for them from crowdfundings if you backer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mouse, Rats ( and later Bunnies ) have <b>Squeeks in the Deep </b>supplement to <b>Pugmire</b> and <b>Mau</b>, so needs one of the corebooks for that. <b>Squeeks </b>do not have 'adventure path' - instead it describe 'mega dungeon' of Underneath, Realms version of Underdark. It has described constant and shifting locations in it.<br /> <br /> And that's all of big, official books for Realms of Pugmire, from what I know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-04-2024, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T17:11:51-08:00","id":1532303,"title":"","content":"As someone who literally just picked up <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> a couple of days ago, skipping Pugmire due to being a cynaphobe, what would be the best support for it? Beyond the <b>Curious Cats</b> book, I'll definitely pick it up at some point but I should be fine on creating adventures.<br /> <br /> I already know people who'll likely be exited to play, as cats make perfect D&amp;D style adventurers and RoP seems to avoid a big issue a lot of people I know have with 5e (the sheer oversaturation of spellcasters).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T23:03:56-08:00","id":1532317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1531906-new-to-pugmire-where-to-start?p=1532303#post1532303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who literally just picked up <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> a couple of days ago, skipping Pugmire (...) what would be the best support for it? Beyond the <b>Curious Cats</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Looking over <b>DriveThruRPG</b> under <i><b>'Monarchies of Mau'</b></i>...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/browse?keyword=Monarchies%20of%20Mau\" target=\"_blank\">https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/...ies%20of%20Mau</a><br /> <br /> May I advert my own work? <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/286176/life-on-the-road\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Life on the Road</b></a> is small collection of house rules for travelling campaigns - I written those for our <b>Adventures for Curious Cats</b> playthrough even, when traveling long days between Houses lands. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But they should help you on ANY <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> land chronicle. Random Encounters rules should also be very useful with coming official <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/episode-289-threats-and-curs-design-diary/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Threats and Curs</b></a> 'monster manual' for <b>RoP</b> in general. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And it only costs 1.0 $! ( From which I get like 0.50 $ of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> rest gets OPP from license. ) / I'm thinking about doing 2E 'print', when 2E <b>RoP</b> corebook will come out, to fix references for new book etc. /<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/286176/life-on-the-road\" target=\"_blank\">https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/...fe-on-the-road</a><br /> <br /> I cannot overstate <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/273857/adventures-for-curious-cats\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Adventures for Curious Cats</b></a> as source for <b>Mau</b> - ( and PDF costs only 3$ now ) - it really is very cool and showing game world chronicle. HOWERVER first adventure takes a half of it in dogs realm, so as cynaphobe you may want to redo it - for example, use other House lands instead of Houndton. ( Probably Siberian as they are <i>'weird, superstitious mountain cat-people'</i>. ) Rest of the chronicle would play smoothly as Cats only material. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/285847/morty-corgi-s-scroll-of-mysteries\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Morty Corgi's Scroll of Mysteries</b></a> is simply THE best <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> fan supplement! It's random tables alone makes it must have - not counting adding the tones of Relics and options! It's like unofficial Player's Guide for other systems. <b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br /> <br /> <br /> '<b>100 (Things)' </b>books are useful for quick location or plots generation. <b>Knicks&amp;Knack</b>s are especially flavour to add to locations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1498_1710054617442_608\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1498\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1498\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1498&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1499_1710054775327_172\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1499\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1499\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1499&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><b><a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/279856/hidden-orders-of-house-mau\" target=\"_blank\">Hidden Orders of House Mau</a> </b>is <i>really</i> House Mau focused things. I would buy it now only if you do Mau ( House ) political game. <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/278322/secret-callings-of-the-shadow-bloc\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Secret Callings of the Shadow Bloc</b></a> is the same for Shadow Bloc high campaign.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/311052/pirates-of-pugmire\" target=\"_blank\">Pirates of Pugmire</a></b> is really good big suplement if you dwell into sea or nautical adventures. Of two described cities in it ( and one secret archipelago ) <i>Water Dog Port</i> have much stronger presence and feel of it. ( Probably cause chronicle in book also takes place there. ) On the other paw <i>Port Matthew</i>, cats mostly city, is a bit under detailed in my opinion. It's still cool location with labyrinths of bridges to walk on for your cats adventure party. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tales of Excellent Cats</b> - fiction anthology - I did not read, so I cannot say anything about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-10-2024, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T22:30:29-07:00","id":1532834,"title":"","content":"HERE we have some sum-ups of <b>Curious Cats of Mau</b> 3 adventures inside book. Grab it of you can right now, <a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/projects/onyx-path/curious-cats-of-mau#top\" target=\"_blank\">BackerKit campaign for it ends in 2 days!</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting Notes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all the excitement about the cool updates to the material we\u2019re doing for <b>Curious Cats of Mau</b>, I wanted to mention that it also contains <i>three </i>entire adventures which comprise a loose campaign! Check these bad boys out!<br /> <br /> <i>Eventide and Dawn<br /> After the characters halt an attempted murder, they\u2019re hired to find out who hired the assassins and why. As they unravel the mystery, they uncover a conspiracy worming its way into the heart of the monarchies. This is an introductory adventure suitable for level 1 characters.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Enemy or Ally<br /> Ally von Rex has learned that the characters are more than capable of disrupting her plans and that of House Smilodon. The only way to ensure they won\u2019t meddle is to take them out. Little does she realize that by trying to deal with them preemptively, she\u2019s given them a clue to her greater scheme. Now she\u2019s trying to enact her plan before the characters catch up to her, and she\u2019s throwing everything she has in their way to destroy them before she fails in her task. \u201cEnemy or Ally\u201d is an adventure for characters at levels 3-4. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Forsaken Shadows Gather<br /> When the heroes discover a plot by House Smilodon to corrupt innocent cats and infiltrate a summit where the monarchies plan to discuss how to face the resurgent Unseen threat of the fallen house, the duty to stop the worst from happening falls upon them. This is a challenging and dangerous adventure, meant for level 5-6 characters.</i><br /> <br /> That means that, using absolutely nothing but the book, you have enough material for an entire campaign of about five to eight sessions. With a little work to come up with missions between those (using the books suggestions of helpful story hooks), you can expand that to take the characters from level 1 to level 6 over a dozen sessions or more, and get them ready for even greater adventures at higher level. It\u2019s an entire campaign book of mystery, intrigue, and dangerous demonic adventure!</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","user":"RichT","date":". 03-19-2024, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}